From 5c703f642f93f2fec9762a3c031020456908845a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mikekinney@Mikes-MacBook-Pro.local>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 02:46:49 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(motion): a step too small to ladder is refused by name,
 never allocated

band() and cut_levels() check the pass count before allocating: a
stepover or stepdown needing more than MAX_PASSES (100000) rows or
levels, or too small to advance the coordinate, is refused as
GenError::Invalid naming the parameter. A 1e-9 mm Face stepover or
Contour stepdown aborted the process on a ~96 GB allocation.

Fixes #691

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL
